<title>USA: Antex Biologics gets OK for Phase I trial.</title>
<headline>Antex Biologics gets OK for Phase I trial.</headline>
<dateline>GAITHERSBURG, Md. 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Antex Biologics Inc said Friday it has received approval from the Food and Drug Administration to begin a clinical study of a vaccine designed to prevent peptic ulcers, gastritis and other related disorders.</p>
<p>The company said it plans to begin a Phase I study of its orally administered Helicobacter pylori vaccine with about 40 volunteers.</p>
<p>The trial is to determine the safety and immunogenicity of the vaccine. But Chairman and Chief Executive Vic Esposito said in a statement the trial may also determine the vaccine's &quot;efficacy as demonstrated by preclinical studies.&quot;</p>
</text>
